mmetric decision function would reason the same way, but I'm also considering how each essay's reading might shift that.\n\nIf the other copy's choice runs on a separate node held at its prior, then defecting dominates, and sending the letter is better whatever the other copy does: 4(1-r) against 2r + 5(1-r) when the other keeps quiet with probability r. Both copies defect at the fixed point, so A-FDT as the essay frames it says to submit. I'm setting aside the argument that identical inputs up to renaming should share one node, since the essay's red/blue example treats differing inputs as distinct, and I'll follow that reading.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing how to decide each essay under the A-FDT framing: the other copy's choice is governed by a separate node held at its prior, while self-consistency requires those priors to match what A-FDT outputs on those inputs. With the two inputs differing only in names and lead content, a symmetric decision function would reason the same way, but I'm also considering how each essay's reading might shift that.\n\nIf the other copy's choice runs on a separate node held at its prior, then defecting dominates, and sending the letter is better whatever the other copy does: 4(1-r) against 2r + 5(1-r) when the other keeps quiet with probability r. Both copies defect at the fixed point, so A-FDT as the essay frames it says to submit. I'm setting aside the argument that identical inputs up to renaming should share one node, since the essay's red/blue example treats differing inputs as distinct, and I'll follow that reading.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9120,"completion_tokens":868,"total_tokens":9988,"cost":0.05384,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05384,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03648,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01736},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":388,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}